<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Pre-grant the runtime location permissions.

     privapp-permissions (org.joan.ims.xml) cannot do this. That file
     allowlists signature|privileged permissions; a dangerous runtime
     permission is neither granted by an entry there nor required to have
     one, so such an entry is simply never consulted. LG's own
     privapp-permissions-lge-joan.xml grants com.lge.ims nine permissions
     and every one is signature|privileged, with no location among them,
     which is the same rule seen from the other side.

     These are used by exactly one thing: getAllCellInfo, so that
     P-Access-Network-Info can carry utran-cell-id-3gpp as TS 24.229
     7.2A.4 and both reference stacks do. joan uses location for nothing
     else, and asking for it is ordinary here rather than novel; LG's
     shipped com.lge.ims 6.1.0.20180701 declares COARSE and FINE, and
     AOSP's ImsStack declares COARSE, FINE and BACKGROUND.

     BACKGROUND is on that list because an ImsService has no UI and is
     always a background process, and since API 29 that needs its own
     grant or the cell cache reads back empty. LG could not have declared
     it: that app targets API 28, where it did not exist.

     NOT here: LOCATION_BYPASS. joan does request it, matching AOSP's
     ImsStack, but it is signature|privileged rather than a runtime
     permission, so it is granted by the privapp allowlist in
     org.joan.ims.xml and this file would never be consulted for it.

     fixed="false" so all of these can be revoked. A revoked grant costs
     one header parameter and nothing else, and the state row then reads
     pani_cell=no-permission.

     VERIFIED NOT TO APPLY to a sideloaded install, which is what this
     package is. DefaultPermissionGrantPolicy.grantDefaultPermissions runs
     on first boot and platform upgrades; there is no path that revisits a
     system package added afterwards. alpha63 shipped this file and the
     tester's state row still read pani_cell=no-permission.

     It is kept because it IS the right mechanism for a ROM that builds
     joan in, or for a device flashed and then wiped. For a sideload, the
     app now asks instead: JoanPermissionActivity is a launcher entry the
     tester opens once. RECORD_AUDIO is not listed here because it is
     requested there rather than pretended at.

     Failing both, and needing no root:
       adb shell pm grant org.joan.ims android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION
       adb shell pm grant org.joan.ims android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION
       adb shell pm grant org.joan.ims android.permission.ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION
-->
<exceptions>
    <exception package="org.joan.ims">
        <permission name="android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" fixed="false"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION" fixed="false"/>
    </exception>
</exceptions>
